  "summary": "At a Fourth Ward meeting, Evanston officials discussed preparations for a federal immigration enforcement operation in Chicago, including proposed legislation against masked federal agents and impersonation. Officer Nate Basner confirmed Evanston PD terminated its Flock Safety ALPR contract over reports of pilot data-sharing with federal law enforcement and is seeking a new vendor; Flock disputes the termination and may sue over the ~$150,000 contract through 2029.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "reports that the private vendor had \"pilot programs\" for sharing data with federal law enforcement persuaded the department to \"decline to further our contract,\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "Unfortunately, due to Flock's misstep, we're going to have to find another ALPR company to get that investigative tool back up and running",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock isn't keen on letting Evanston terminate its contract, which calls for the city to pay nearly $150,000 for service through January 2029.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
  ],
